    "html_url": "https://github.com/advisories/GHSA-mrhx-c7xc-m3w5",
    "summary": "Zod can exhaust memory while validating oversized constrained collections",
    "description": "Zod schema-validation library through 4.6.5 contains an uncontrolled resource consumption vulnerability that allows attackers to exhaust memory by submitting a large array to an application using an array schema without a length constraint. Attackers can exploit the handleArrayResult parse logic in $ZodArray, which accumulates every validation issue for each failing element with no cap or early termination, causing the process to allocate excessive issue objects and crash due to out-of-memory conditions.",
    "type": "reviewed",
    "severity": "high",
